{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>Set your heart.</b> A person needs his eyes and his heart and his ears directed to the words of Torah — and so it says: ״Son of man, see with your eyes and with your ears hear, and set your heart״ (Ezekiel 40). And this is a kal va-chomer: if for the plan of the Temple, which is visible to the eyes and measured by a measuring reed, a person needs his eyes and ears and heart directed — to understand the words of Torah, which are suspended by a hair, how much the more so (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:31.466790432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}